<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- ROT_FLORA_FAUNA_VERDICTS_1 — owner ruling 2026-09-19, applied provisionally
       (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/rot_flora_fauna_names.md /
       design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/rot_regen_briefs.json). Renames + resizes the 12 RM_ flora
       defs (ported from Alpha Biomes' Plants_MycoticJungle.xml) to the Rot's own
       campaign names and ruled mature widths.

       The fauna half (7 Alpha Animals donors: AA_Agaripawn, AA_Agaripod,
       AA_AngelMoth, AA_MycoidColossus, AA_Swarmling, AA_Wildpawn, AA_Wildpod)
       was deleted by ROTNAMES_PRUNE_DONOR_OPS_LIVE_ABSENT, 2026-10-25: Alpha
       Animals is retired and none of those defs is in the live game. Each one's
       name, size and art now live on its owned RM_ port (RM_Agaripawn,
       RM_Agaripod, RM_Dustveil, RM_MycoidColossus, RM_Chittik, RM_Durrok,
       RM_Mullgoth) — edit there, never here.

       ⛔ NO MayRequire on an Operation — inert, and already the standing lesson
       in this file's own sibling PlantTolerances_Ashkarr.xml. Each def's block
       below is gated by PatchOperationConditional on the ThingDef's own xpath:
       if the donor mod is absent the outer Conditional's xpath simply does not
       match and the whole block no-ops — no MayRequire needed, no error logged,
       and no dependency on knowing the donor's exact ModContentPack.Name (which
       PatchOperationFindMod matches against, not packageId).

       Sizes: flora <plant><visualSizeRange> MAX set to the ruled width, MIN
       scaled to keep the def's own existing min:max ratio. -->

  <!-- ============== RM_AgaricusDomeCap -> skarrowdome (7 wide) ============== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_AgaricusDomeCap"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_AgaricusDomeCap"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>skarrowdome</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_AgaricusDomeCap"]/description</xpath>
          <value><description>A squat, swollen dome of a mushroom as wide as a hut, its skin blotched in the yellows and bruise-purples that every other living thing reads as a warning. People read it as an invitation. Under the skin lies a pale psychotropic flesh, cut away a sliver at a time: one sliver opens the mind, two take it somewhere it does not come back from easily. It grows slowly, and each skarrowdome gives up very little.</description></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_AgaricusDomeCap"]/plant/visualSizeRange</xpath>
          <value><visualSizeRange>5.25~7</visualSizeRange></value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ============== RM_AgariluxPrime -> grath elder (20 wide) ============== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_AgariluxPrime"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_AgariluxPrime"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>grath elder</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_AgariluxPrime"]/description</xpath>
          <value><description>An elder of the pale forest, twenty paces across and older than any settlement on the planet. It never stops breathing: a standing cloud of heavy, suffocating spores rolls out from under its cap and settles around it, and anything that wanders in, whether grazer, hunter, colonist or rival fungus, chokes, lies down and does not get up. Then the slow part starts. Pale hyphae creep out from its foot to the bodies and eat them where they lie. Do not walk into its shadow. Anyone who means to cut one must be sealed against its breath to the last seam; a mortar, from far enough away, works better.</description></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_AgariluxPrime"]/plant/visualSizeRange</xpath>
          <value><visualSizeRange>19.88~20</visualSizeRange></value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ============== RM_ArbuscularMycorrhiza -> madruka (9 wide) ============== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_ArbuscularMycorrhiza"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_ArbuscularMycorrhiza"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>madruka</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_ArbuscularMycorrhiza"]/description</xpath>
          <value><description>A fungus that long ago swallowed a tree and kept its bones. The madruka's trunk is still wood, ridged, pale and cold to the touch, but everything above it is mushroom: a broad cap where the crown should be, gills where the leaves once grew, and a mycelium that runs far underground. Cutting one yields a good stack of real wood, and it can be planted and grown again.</description></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_ArbuscularMycorrhiza"]/plant/visualSizeRange</xpath>
          <value><visualSizeRange>5.14~9</visualSizeRange></value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ============== RM_Bryolux -> hessuk moss (unchanged size) ============== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_Bryolux"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_Bryolux"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>hessuk moss</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_Bryolux"]/description</xpath>
          <value><description>The glow-carpet of the pale forest: a blue-white mat of tangled sticky fibres, warm to lie on and slow to walk through, because it holds your feet. Where it is bright the ground is feeding; where it goes dark, the ground is cold.</description></value>
        </li>
        <!-- Draw order (owner, 2026-10-14): the moss is ground cover and must always sit UNDER the
             mushrooms. The donor put it on Building (15), above every LowPlant (11) mushroom; and a
             plant's top edge is raised 0.1 (Plant.Print, topVerticesAltitudeBias) against 0.0366
             between layers, so a moss only 3 layers below (FloorEmplacement 7) is guaranteed lower. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_Bryolux"]/altitudeLayer</xpath>
          <value><altitudeLayer>FloorEmplacement</altitudeLayer></value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

